# Owner review for the files that decide whether CI can fail, and for the
# contract this repository does not own.
#
# docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md and ADR-002 § "Branch protection and rulesets"
# (item 7) require owner review on workflows, gate scripts and the
# required-check manifest. A manifest edited in the same PR as the code it
# guards defeats the gate, which is exactly what this file exists to prevent.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS is only advisory until a ruleset requires owner review on
# these paths. Applying that ruleset is an owner action (ADR-002 item 9:
# "application happens after PR1 lands, because ci-required must exist before
# it can be required") and is NOT part of this pull request.

# Everything in this repository, as the baseline.
*                           @yegamble

# CI definition, the required-check manifest and the fan-in gate.
/.github/                   @yegamble
/.github/workflows/         @yegamble
/.github/required-checks.txt @yegamble
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @yegamble

# The gate scripts: `make ci` defines every required lane.
/Makefile                   @yegamble

# The canonical contract, vendored from vizra-core and not ours to edit, plus
# the manifest that pins the commit and digest it came from.
/api/                       @yegamble

# The security boundary itself.
/internal/hmacauth/         @yegamble
/internal/config/           @yegamble

# The engineering contract for this repository.
/AGENTS.md                  @yegamble
/CLAUDE.md                  @yegamble
